Ok, I've got a workaround for you, it's a bit of a hack, but I haven't come
across any other way of getting the data into Audacity.  Winamp makes a
pretty good transcoder, go to preferences->Plugins->Output-> Nullsoft Disk
Writer plug-in  and hit Configure.  Set the output dir and check the
'convert to format' box and select PCM as the format then the bottom choice
as the attributes.  Close all the open settings windows, make a playlist of
things to be transcoded and hit play.  The resulting wav files will work
fine in audacity.  Once the editing is done getting them back to flac
shouldn't be too difficult.

--teyret



